{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-13 17:48:03 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-14 00:48:03 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\n**Verdict: request changes.** Three reproduced contract gaps:\n\n| Severity | File:line | Invariant/evidence | Recommended correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P1 | [linearize.cljc:177](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linearize.cljc:177) | §2.5 permits literal maps; §5.1 defines `lower-ast` as composition. The unrestricted tree walk rejects `{:type :literal :value {:type :vm/store-update}}`, although `lower` accepts its datoms. | Traverse only structural AST children. Treat literal values and other data operands as opaque. Add parity regressions for both unsupported keywords inside literals. |\n| P2 | [linearize.cljc:147](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linearize.cljc:147) | Custom tempids bypass collision and negative-integer checks. With literal root `-17`, `:id-start -16` assigns instruction `-17`, merging AST/code identities when transacted together. `:id-start 1` emits IDs `1, 0, -1`. | Validate the entire allocated range: negative integers, distinct IDs, and no overlap with input entities. Add invalid-option regressions. |\n| P1 | [linearize.cljc:58](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linearize.cljc:58) | §2.5 prohibits host functions in code datoms. A literal containing `{:nested [f]}` preserves the identical host function; `well-formed?` accepts it. Store values are also copied unchecked. | Enforce the plain-data boundary recursively for emitted data operands; reject host functions/objects with source-node evidence. Resolve primitives through symbolic `:var` instructions. |\n\nProperties that passed review:\n\n- Every emitted instruction receives its originating AST eid; synthetic `halt` and `return` reference the root and lambda respectively. Segment provenance names the root.\n- Default allocation uses noncolliding negative tempids. Output uses canonical five-tuples, the requested transaction, and default metadata.\n- Actual `:yin/macro-expand` and `:vm/store-update` nodes are rejected with node-identifying errors.\n- Labels resolve to instruction entities within the emitted segment. PCs are dense and ordered; main code ends in `halt`, and out-of-line bodies end in `return`.\n- Lowering follows §5.3 evaluation order and preserves call tail annotations.\n- No hidden global or shared mutable state: compilation atoms are invocation-local. Lowering remains separate from loading/execution and constructs its index explicitly from tuples.\n\nValidation: **10 tests, 398 assertions passed under Babashka**, plus focused reproductions above. JVM/CLJS/CLJD runs were not performed. No files changed."}}
